# Argo CD / Argo Workflows desired state for business apps.
*            @Ubuntu-25c-market-prep/argocd @Ubuntu-25c-market-prep/cto

# The AppProject and the ApplicationSets are the security boundary itself, not
# an application of it: projects/business.yaml decides what every business app
# is allowed to do, and applicationsets/ decides which Applications exist at all.
#
# ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING: CODEOWNERS is last-matching-pattern-wins, so these
# entries MUST stay BELOW the `*` line above. Moved above it they match nothing
# and the control disappears silently - which is what has already happened to
# every per-directory entry in gitops-flux and infra-aws. See ops-program#48.
/projects/           @Ubuntu-25c-market-prep/cto
/applicationsets/    @Ubuntu-25c-market-prep/cto

# The per-cluster entrypoints. Adding a directory here is how a cluster starts
# reconciling anything at all, and which environments it is allowed to run is
# decided by the resource list inside it - so a new prod cluster is a @cto
# review, not a folder someone creates in passing. See ADR 0014.
/clusters/           @Ubuntu-25c-market-prep/cto
# Prod overlays need @cto specifically, not just @argocd.
#
# ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING: CODEOWNERS is last-matching-pattern-wins, so this entry
# MUST stay BELOW the `*` line above. Moved above it, it matches nothing and this
# control silently disappears - which is exactly what has happened to every
# per-directory entry in gitops-flux and infra-aws. See ops-program#48.
#
# This narrows prod review to @cto rather than widening it. That is deliberate:
# it is the third of the three controls on a production release, alongside the
# absent syncPolicy and the Argo RBAC. See docs/promotion.md.
/apps/*/overlays/prod/    @Ubuntu-25c-market-prep/cto

